<tr><td colspan=4><font size=2 face=verdana color=#ffffff>Entry #1<p>
A little about myself and how I came to be who I am today.  <p>

I was just a seemingly average elf at first glance, maybe aspiring to be a merchant or smith of some sort.  But beyond my pleasant demeanor lied a tormented soul.  
<p>
My father was a drunkard who would hang by the local tavern and use all of our hard earned gold peices on elven ale.  He would beat my mother after I carried him out of the local Tavern.  I was only of fourteen years when my mother took her life, she left me her life's savings and a small note.
<p>
"Please son, do not be angry with me.  I have suffered enough and I know it is time to relieve myself of my pain.  I am off to a better place, with Tunare perhaps.  Do not let your father rule over you..." 
<p>
My mother's death was the tip of the ice so to speak, I went completely insane, that night after carrying my father home (there was no beating of course because my mother was dead...) I purchased a rusty weapon and slid it into his chest.  He was far too drunk to notice that I had just killed him.
<p>
I was ashamed and fled into the wilderness, foraging for grapes and water pods to survive.  Suprisingly coming back to the city to buy some ale and drink my problems away.
<p>
One day I tried to drink myself into oblivion.  I was near death when I saw the beautiful face of Tunare.
<p>
"WHAT HAVE YOU DONE WITH YOURSELF NILAMIEN!" she screamed with the rage of a tempest wind.
<p>
"DO YOU REALIZE WHO YOU HAVE BECOME?!" she continued. I thought I was halucinating until she slapped my face...
<p>
"Do you honestly think this is what your mother had in mind?" her voice softened and became very melodious.  It instantly seemed I had been filtered of the alcohal.  I blushed in shame,
<p>
"I have no idea what I am to do..." I began to walk away sheepishly.
<p>
"My child, you had no choice, come with me and I will give your life meaning" I followed her as she ordered.  She led me back to the city and to a small building that said, "Faydarks Champions".  She introduced me to all of the local mercenaries and my interest grew in their profession.  They were all rangers of Tunare.  I signed up immediately.  I rose through the ranks quite rapidly.  I started off as pest control killing sall things in the city, bugs, bats, the usual, nothing too hard of course.  Then I was upgraded to Pixie Patrol.  This made me a large amount of money.  I became quite popular with the locals eventually.
<p>
Then the day came where I was upgraded to Orc Eliminator.  What a challenge, I had a blood thirst like no other.  I killed with ease.  Soon enough I went to Crush Bone which was even more exciting.
<p>
Now I can stroll into Crush Bone with ease and not be afriad of anything.  My journey has just begun.
<p>
Entry #2
<p>
  I have begun a journey to oasis where I plan to kill many crocs with a new sword I purchased from a friend.  People are more kinder and a lot less noisier then i expected.  I have already increased three levels and cant wait to report back to Faydarks Champions to tell them of my progress.
<p>
Nil
